# ClarityAnchor environment configuration
# Copy to `.env.local` (gitignored). Everything here is OPTIONAL — with no config
# the app runs on a built-in, credential-free heuristic model for demos.
#
# This project uses AWS Bedrock as its only LLM provider. Add AWS credentials
# below and the app auto-detects them and drives the agent with Bedrock.

# ── Amazon Bedrock credentials (any ONE of these) ────────────────────────────
#   a) IAM keys:
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=...
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=...
# AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=...            # only if using temporary/STS credentials
#   b) Bedrock API key (simplest):
# AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK=...
#   c) or `aws configure` / `aws sso login` / an instance role (no vars needed)

# ── Bedrock options ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AWS_REGION=us-west-2                                  # default us-west-2
# BEDROCK_MODEL_ID=global.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6  # enable model access first
#
# Force the offline heuristic even when AWS creds are present:
# MODEL_PROVIDER=mock

# ── Demo pacing ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Artificial delay (ms) between heuristic tool steps so the live map is watchable.
# Ignored by the real Bedrock model; set to 0 for the crispest real-model runs.
# DEMO_LATENCY_MS=650
